IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`
IMPORT `s121-d9-service`
IMPORT `s121-whole`
IMPORT `s121-seat`

-- LAYER 2 worked cases: one or more for every question of the seat, on the facts a taxpayer would state.
-- Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text and the calendar, written beside the assertion, then run.
-- Sale on 15 March 2026 unless stated: the 5-year period is 16 March 2021 to 15 March 2026 (1826 days) and 2 years is 730 days (16 March 2024 to 15 March 2026).
-- "enter any date" in a question means the date is read only if the yes/no answer before it is yes: those cases give 1 January 1900.
-- Arguments follow the order of the question's inputs in s121-seat.l4.

§ `The two-year tests`

-- Owner from 1 January 2015, lived there from then until the sale: well over 2 years: yes
#ASSERT `Have I owned and lived in my home long enough` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one year of each: no
#ASSERT `Have I owned and lived in my home long enough` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- exactly 730 days owned and lived in (16 March 2024 to 15 March 2026): yes; one day less (from 17 March 2024): no
#ASSERT `Have I owned and lived in my home long enough` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2024) (Date 16 3 2024) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I owned and lived in my home long enough` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2024) (Date 17 3 2024) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- two stays: 16 March 2021 to 15 March 2022 (365 days) and 16 March 2025 to 15 March 2026 (365 days) make 730 aggregated: yes
#ASSERT `Have I owned and lived in my home long enough` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 16 3 2021) (Date 15 3 2022) TRUE (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a first stay wholly before the 5-year period (1 January 2015 to 31 December 2020) adds nothing: 365 days in it: no
#ASSERT `Have I owned and lived in my home long enough` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 31 12 2020) TRUE (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (d)(9): called to duty in the uniformed services from 1 January 2018 to the sale; elects: the 5-year period begins 1 January 2013
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `member of the uniformed services` FALSE 100 FALSE TRUE 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 1 1 2013
-- no election: the ordinary 5-year period begins on 16 March 2021
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `member of the uniformed services` FALSE 100 FALSE TRUE 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 16 3 2021
-- another election is already in effect: it may not be made
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `member of the uniformed services` FALSE 100 FALSE TRUE 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 16 3 2021
-- the duty station is 49 miles away and no Government quarters: not qualified official extended duty, so no days are suspended
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `member of the uniformed services` FALSE 49 FALSE TRUE 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 16 3 2021
-- exactly 50 miles away: qualified
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `member of the uniformed services` FALSE 50 FALSE TRUE 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 1 1 2013
-- a call for exactly 90 days is not "in excess of 90 days": no days are suspended; for 91 days it is
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `member of the uniformed services` FALSE 100 FALSE TRUE 90 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 16 3 2021
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `member of the uniformed services` FALSE 100 FALSE TRUE 91 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 1 1 2013
-- a Peace Corps volunteer serving outside the United States (d)(12): the same extension
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `enrolled volunteer or volunteer leader under the Peace Corps Act` TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `some other office` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Date 1 1 2013
-- the same volunteer serving inside the United States: nothing is suspended
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `enrolled volunteer or volunteer leader under the Peace Corps Act` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `some other office` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Date 16 3 2021
-- an intelligence-community employee of the Central Intelligence Agency, on qualified extended duty: the extension
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `employee of the intelligence community` FALSE 100 FALSE TRUE 4000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the Central Intelligence Agency` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 1 1 2013
-- a capacity the text does not name: nothing is suspended
#ASSERT `On what date does my 5-year period begin` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 15 3 2026) `some other capacity` FALSE 100 FALSE TRUE 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Date 16 3 2021

§ `Joint returns, an earlier sale, and a surviving spouse`

-- (b)(3): an earlier sale on 14 March 2025 is within the 2 years ending 15 March 2026: it bars
#ASSERT `Does an earlier sale stop me leaving this gain out` (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an earlier sale on 15 March 2024 is one day before the 2-year period begins: no bar
#ASSERT `Does an earlier sale stop me leaving this gain out` (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE (Date 15 3 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- on 16 March 2024, the first day of the period: bars
#ASSERT `Does an earlier sale stop me leaving this gain out` (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE (Date 16 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no earlier sale
#ASSERT `Does an earlier sale stop me leaving this gain out` (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (b)(4): the spouse died on 1 March 2025; the home was owned and lived in by both from 1 January 2015; the sale on 15 March 2026 is within 2 years of the death: $500,000
#ASSERT `Is my limit 500,000 as a surviving spouse` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 28 2 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the sale is on 2 March 2027, one day after the 2 years: no
#ASSERT `Is my limit 500,000 as a surviving spouse` (Date 2 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 2 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 28 2 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- on 1 March 2027, the last day: yes
#ASSERT `Is my limit 500,000 as a surviving spouse` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 28 2 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the late spouse lived in the home only from 1 March 2024: 365 days of the 5 years before death, so both spouses did not meet the use requirement: no
#ASSERT `Is my limit 500,000 as a surviving spouse` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 28 2 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I sold another home on 1 June 2023, within 2 years before the death: paragraph (3) bars me, so (b)(2)(A)(iii) was not met: no
#ASSERT `Is my limit 500,000 as a surviving spouse` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 6 2023) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 28 2 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- joint return: I own and we both live in it since 2015: $500,000
#ASSERT `What is the most of our gain we can leave out filing jointly` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST 500000
-- my spouse lived there only 365 days of the 5 years: $250,000 (mine) plus $0 (my spouse's)
#ASSERT `What is the most of our gain we can leave out filing jointly` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST 250000
-- my spouse never lived there: same
#ASSERT `What is the most of our gain we can leave out filing jointly` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST 250000
-- my spouse sold another home on 14 March 2025: paragraph (3) bars them, so (b)(2)(A)(iii) fails: $250,000
#ASSERT `What is the most of our gain we can leave out filing jointly` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST 250000

§ `The reduced exclusion`

-- one year in the home, sold for a change of employment: (c) applies
#ASSERT `Does the reduced exclusion apply to my sale` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- with health: applies; with unforeseen circumstances the regulations count: applies
#ASSERT `Does the reduced exclusion apply to my sale` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the reduced exclusion apply to my sale` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no reason: it does not
#ASSERT `Does the reduced exclusion apply to my sale` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an owner since 2015 has met the tests, so (c) is not needed, whatever the reason
#ASSERT `Does the reduced exclusion apply to my sale` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an owner since 2015 barred by a sale on 14 March 2025, selling for health: (c) applies
#ASSERT `Does the reduced exclusion apply to my sale` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- the limit: one year, change of employment: 365 of 730 days, so half of $250,000
#ASSERT `What is the most of my gain I can leave out filing alone` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST 125000
-- 2 days short of 2 years: 728 days owned and lived in (18 March 2024 to 15 March 2026): 728/730 of 250,000
#ASSERT `What is the most of my gain I can leave out filing alone` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 18 3 2024) (Date 18 3 2024) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST (250000 TIMES (728 DIVIDED BY 730))
-- an earlier sale on 14 March 2025 and a health reason: the shorter of 1826 and 365 days: half of $250,000
#ASSERT `What is the most of my gain I can leave out filing alone` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST 125000
-- the tests met: the full $250,000
#ASSERT `What is the most of my gain I can leave out filing alone` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST 250000
-- the tests failed and no reason: nothing can be left out, limit $0
#ASSERT `What is the most of my gain I can leave out filing alone` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST 0

§ `Part of the time not my home, and depreciation`

-- (d)(6): 40,000 of depreciation taken after May 6, 1997 on a gain of 200,000: 40,000 of the gain is taxed
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of depreciation` (Date 15 3 2026) 200000 40000 EQUALS JUST 40000
-- more depreciation than gain: all of the gain
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of depreciation` (Date 15 3 2026) 200000 300000 EQUALS JUST 200000
-- none
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of depreciation` (Date 15 3 2026) 200000 0 EQUALS JUST 0

-- (b)(5): owned 16 March 2016 to the sale (3652 days), lived in it from 16 March 2021 (1826 days): half the gain of 200,000 is allocated to nonqualified use
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of nonqualified use` (Date 15 3 2026) 200000 (Date 16 3 2016) (Date 16 3 2021) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 100000
-- the same with 40,000 of depreciation first: half of 160,000
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of nonqualified use` (Date 15 3 2026) 200000 (Date 16 3 2016) (Date 16 3 2021) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) 40000 FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 80000
-- an owner-occupier since 2015: no nonqualified use
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of nonqualified use` (Date 15 3 2026) 200000 (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- before January 1, 2009 does not count: owned from 1 January 2000, lived in it from 1 January 2009: no nonqualified use
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of nonqualified use` (Date 15 3 2026) 200000 (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2009) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- one day later: lived in it from 2 January 2009, so 1 January 2009 alone is nonqualified use: 1 day of 9571 owned
-- Hand count of 1 January 2000 to 15 March 2026: 26 x 365 = 9490; leap days 2000, 2004, 2008, 2012, 2016, 2020, 2024 = 7; 9497 to 31 December 2025; plus 74 days of 2026; 9571. A gain of 957,100 allocates 957,100 / 9571 = 100.
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of nonqualified use` (Date 15 3 2026) 957100 (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 2 1 2009) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
-- a temporary absence for health of one year, 16 March 2016 to 15 March 2017, within the nonqualified use: the exception takes 365 days of the 1826, leaving 1461 of 3652 owned: on a gain of 365,200, 146,100
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of nonqualified use` (Date 15 3 2026) 365200 (Date 16 3 2016) (Date 16 3 2021) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) 0 TRUE (Date 16 3 2016) (Date 15 3 2017) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 146100
-- the same absence with no reason the text names: no exception, half of 365,200
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of nonqualified use` (Date 15 3 2026) 365200 (Date 16 3 2016) (Date 16 3 2021) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) 0 TRUE (Date 16 3 2016) (Date 15 3 2017) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 182600
-- a gain of 0 allocates 0
#ASSERT `How much of my gain is taxed because of nonqualified use` (Date 15 3 2026) 0 (Date 16 3 2016) (Date 16 3 2021) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0

