§ `Things that take my sale out of the section`

-- Arguments: sale, what happened, elect not (f), 877(a)(1), like-kind exchange, seller is me, date acquired, remainder interest, elect (d)(8)(A), another interest sold separately, related person.
-- an ordinary sale with none of them: the section reaches it
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I elect not to have the section apply: it does not
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- section 877(a)(1) applies to me: it does not
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I got the home in a like-kind exchange on 1 June 2023: within 5 years of the sale: it does not; on 1 June 2020 (5 years ended 31 May 2025): it does
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a sale on 31 May 2025 of a home got on 1 June 2020: 31 May 2025 is the last day of the 5 years beginning 1 June 2020, so it is barred; on 1 June 2025 it is not
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 31 5 2025) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 1 6 2025) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the like-kind exchange was by someone whose basis is not mine: (d)(10) does not speak
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 6 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- another interest in the home was sold separately: it does not
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a remainder interest, with the election, to someone unrelated: the section reaches it
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a remainder interest without the election: the text does not say (not covered)
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a remainder interest sold to a related person: the election does not apply; the text does not say the section fails to apply (not covered)
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `sale or exchange` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the home was condemned: treated as a sale: the section reaches it; some other event: not covered
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `condemnation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` (Date 15 3 2026) `some other event` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (d)(5)(A): each listed event is treated as a sale; a sale is a sale; anything else is not covered
#ASSERT `Is what happened to my home treated as a sale` `destruction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what happened to my home treated as a sale` `theft` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what happened to my home treated as a sale` `seizure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what happened to my home treated as a sale` `requisition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what happened to my home treated as a sale` `condemnation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what happened to my home treated as a sale` `sale or exchange` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what happened to my home treated as a sale` `some other event` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (d)(5)(B): 1,000,000 realized, 250,000 not included in gross income by reason of section 121: 750,000
#ASSERT `What is the amount realized for section 1033` 1000000 250000 EQUALS 750000

